          "blocks": {}
        },
        "ai_gen_block_0029bb1_TrydqX": {
          "type": "ai_gen_block_0029bb1",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "How cut affects diamond colour",
            "text": "<p>A diamond’s cut can change how its colour is seen. Round brilliant diamonds tend to disguise subtle warmth more effectively than many other shapes, as their faceting is designed to maximise light return and brilliance.</p><p>By contrast, cuts with broader, more open facets, such as emerald cuts, can make faint colour more visible.</p>",
            "heading_size_desktop": 30,
            "text_size_desktop": 18,
            "padding_left_desktop": 380,
            "padding_right_desktop": 380,
            "spacing_desktop": 40,
            "heading_size_mobile": 20,
            "text_size_mobile": 14,
            "padding_left_mobile": 40,
            "padding_right_mobile": 40,
            "spacing_mobile": 20,
            "text_alignment": "center",
            "heading_color": "#000000",
            "text_color": "#000000"
          },
          "blocks": {}
        },
        "ai_gen_block_8322f0f_BPMLWb": {
          "type": "ai_gen_block_8322f0f",
          "settings": {
            "padding_top_desktop": 0,
            "padding_bottom_desktop": 25,
            "padding_top_mobile": 5,
            "padding_bottom_mobile": 20
          },
          "blocks": {}
        },
        "ai_gen_block_0029bb1_BNPCFt": {
          "type": "ai_gen_block_0029bb1",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "How carat size impacts diamond colour",
            "text": "<p>Carat weight can also influence colour perception. Larger diamonds have more visible surface area, which can make subtle warmth easier to detect. For this reason, higher colour grades are often preferred as diamond size increases, particularly if a colourless or near-colourless look is desired.</p><p>When choosing a diamond, colour should be considered alongside shape, setting, and carat weight, as each can affect the final appearance of the stone.</p><p>We can help you understand these details and select a diamond with the right balance of colour, beauty, and value. Every diamond is carefully assessed against the 4Cs, including the grading standards set by the Gemological Institute of America (GIA).</p>",
            "heading_size_desktop": 30,
            "text_size_desktop": 18,
            "padding_left_desktop": 380,
            "padding_right_desktop": 380,
            "spacing_desktop": 40,
            "heading_size_mobile": 20,
            "text_size_mobile": 14,
            "padding_left_mobile": 40,
            "padding_right_mobile": 40,
            "spacing_mobile": 20,
